diff --git a/docs/live-game.md b/docs/live-game.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6b46052
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/live-game.md
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# Live game implementation notes
+
+- A quiz run is a separate `games` row with a random five-character join code. Starting a run snapshots only active questions and their options into `game_questions` / `game_options`, so later moderator edits do not alter an in-progress game and two runs never share players or answers.
+- The game moves through `waiting -> open -> closed -> open ... -> over`. Moderator actions are conditional database updates; the final `Next` action ends the run. An all-inactive quiz cannot be started.
+- Player identities are anonymous. A random per-player token is held in an HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax cookie scoped to that game's URL. Re-opening a join link resumes the player; a game that is over never creates a new player.
+- Player answer reads are deliberately separate from moderator result reads. While a question is open, player JSON contains only option IDs and text, the player's selected option, and the question. It has no correctness field or answer totals. The moderator result endpoint only includes correctness and per-option totals after `Finish`.
+- Moderator and player pages use small no-cache JSON polls and update their DOM in place, with a short retry cadence to recover from Wi-Fi interruptions. The QR code is rendered locally as SVG from the same HTTP join URL shown as text; the app does not call an external QR or other service.
+- All persisted game state is in the same SQLite database under `storage/`; the release/start path builds dependencies offline.
diff --git a/src/live.rs b/src/live.rs
